meta {
  name: Delete Account
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/me/account
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Permanently delete the authenticated account. Schedules deletion: marks the user and
  tenant as deletion_pending, revokes all Supabase sessions, and enqueues an asynchronous
  purge job that deletes documents, chunks, vector embeddings, files, conversations,
  shares, tenant keys, and Redis state — while retaining payment history and audit logs.
  Re-registering with the same email afterwards creates a brand-new clean account.

  AUTH IS COOKIE-BASED: the session cookie is sent automatically by the Cookie Jar — no
  Authorization header needed. No request body required.

  Returns 202 (accepted) with { "scheduled": true, "jobId": "..." }.
  While the purge runs, the user's still-valid JWTs are rejected via a Redis tombstone.
}
